# Tables: Overflow shrink in cells of a fixed height reduces the text that does not fit, down to Min size.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Tables · Shrinking text in a cell
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For element: Cell
			Box:
				Height: 22
				Border: 0 0 0.5 0
				Border color: rule
				Overflow: shrink
			Typography:
				Line height: 120%
				Min size: 6
		For element: Header cell
			Typography:
				Bold: true
	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Shrinking text in a cell
		Paragraph: The cells have a fixed `Height` of 22 and `Overflow: shrink`. Their `Line height` is a percentage, so it shrinks with the text. A name that does not fit in its cell is set smaller, half a point at a time, until it fits, without going below `Min size`. Without `Overflow: shrink` the same name would stop the conversion with an error.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: 100 280
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Badge
					Cell: Name
